        {
          "question": "e-7657",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{x}-5 & >0 \\\\ 4{e}^{x} & >5 \\\\ {e}^{x} & >\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({e}^{x}) & >\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(\\frac{5}{4}) \\\\ x & >\\operatorname{ln}\u20615-\\operatorname{ln}\u20614.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981653/example-7657.json",
          "file_sha256": "69bd112804b1d41c9445f39fb981c3c57ed53766198ce14104690b0276cb8157"
